ext":"⚙️ Chemical Engineering"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Process engineering"},{"text":"Mass transfer"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Process control"},{"text":"Industrial safety"}]},{"type":"h","text":"🤖 Future"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Chemometrics"},{"text":"Python/data analysis"},{"text":"AI-assisted analytical testing"},{"text":"Laboratory automation"},{"text":"PAT"},{"text":"Digital laboratories"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Graduate Profile"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally be able to demonstrate:"},{"type":"p","text":"“I understand chemical engineering processes and can perform and document analytical testing, interpret laboratory data, work with common analytical instruments, follow GMP/GLP procedures, investigate quality deviations and use digital laboratory and statistical tools to support reliable product quality.”"},{"type":"p","text":"For Chemical Engineering → Quality Control Chemist, the biggest differentiator is to deliberately add analytical chemistry + hands-on laboratory instrumentation + quality-system knowledge to the core engineering curriculum."}]}]}